## Tests

```bash
pytest modules/{{ module }}/tests
```

`test_{{ module }}_domain.py` needs nothing. `test_{{ module }}_use_cases.py`
needs an event loop and the in-memory adapter. Neither needs PostgreSQL — if
one starts to, something has crossed the port.

## Migration

```bash
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add {{ table }}"
alembic upgrade head
```

Read the generated migration before applying it. Autogenerate misses
server-side defaults, enum changes and index renames.

